    "description": {
      "chat": "",
      "unidentified": "",
      "value": "<p>Choose one creature from the 9th-level list, 1d3 creatures of the same kind from the 8th-level list, or 1d4+1 creatures of the same kind using any combination of lower-level lists. One suitable corpse is required per creature.</p><p>The 9th-level list allows: banshee or shade from a humanoid of CR 8; crypt fiend from a nerubian of CR 11 or 12; forsaken from a humanoid of CR 11; ghoul or wraith from a humanoid or monstrous humanoid of CR 10; skeletal mage from a humanoid of CR 10; skeletal warrior from a humanoid or monstrous humanoid of CR 11; withered from an aberration, animal, dragon, fey, magical beast, plant, or other monstrous creature of CR 10; or ghost from an aberration, animal, giant, humanoid, magical beast, monstrous humanoid, or plant of Charisma 6+ and CR 7. A summoned ghost has malevolence, horrific appearance, and corrupting gaze.</p><p>Summons act immediately on your turn and obey communicated directions. They do not count against your control limit, cannot fuel <em>death pact</em>, summon or conjure, teleport, or travel between planes, and require a supporting environment. At the end, they collapse or vanish and leave remains unusable for further undead magic; every source corpse is despoiled.</p><p><strong>Automation boundary:</strong> Roll the quantity, choose valid lower tiers, validate and consume every corpse, create and control each temporary undead, and remove all summons and unusable remains manually.</p>"
    },
